# Playwright run artifacts (failure traces, HTML report).
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Crawl artifacts: generated by `npm run crawl` (or the prebuild guard),
# baked into the deployed site — never committed.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and that slash is load-bearing. A bare `data/`
# is unanchored: it matches a directory named `data` at ANY depth, and it
# silently swallowed `src/pages/data/` — the build-time endpoint the programme
# typeahead fetches. The file never reached git, so a fresh clone built a site
# whose first-run screen could not find a single studieprogram, while every
# working tree that already had the file kept passing. `public/data/` contains
# a slash and was therefore already anchored; only the first line was wrong.
/data/
/public/data/

# Requests served live because no fixture matched — the global teardown
# reads this and fails the run, then clears it.
e2e/fixtures/.misses
